COMMAND NAME: mppcreatecluster.sh

Initializes a Bizgres MPP system by using configuration 
parameters specified in a MPP configuration file.

*****************************************************
SYNOPSIS
*****************************************************

mppcreatecluster.sh -c <mpp_config_file> [-h <host_file>] 
[-p <postgresql_conf_mpp_additions>] [-s standby_master_host] [-i] 
[-o] [-m <max_connections>] [-a] [-q] [-l <logfile_directory>]

mppcreatecluster.sh [-? | -v]


*****************************************************
DESCRIPTION
*****************************************************

The mppcreatecluster.sh script will create a Bizgres MPP DBMS instance 
using the values defined in a Bizgres MPP configuration file. 
See the 'mpp_config_example' file for instructions on creating this file.
The functionality of mppcreatecluster.sh is analogous to PostgreSQLs 
initdb script, which creates the data storage directories, generates the 
shared catalog tables and configuration files, and creates a template 
database, which is a template used to create other databases. 

In a Bizgres MPP DBMS, each database instance (the master and all segments) 
must be initialized across all of the hosts in the system in such a way that 
they can all work together as a unified DBMS. The mppcreatecluster.sh script 
takes care of initializing the database on the MPP master and on each segment 
instance, and configuring the system as a whole.

Before running mppcreatecluster.sh, you must set the $MPPHOME or $BIZHOME 
environment variable to point to the location of your Bizgres MPP 
installation on the master host.

This script performs the following tasks:

* Verifies that the parameters in the MPP configuration file are correct.
* Ensures that a connection can be established to each host. 
  If a host cannot be reached, the script will exit.
* Displays the configuration that will be used and prompts the user for 
  confirmation.
* Initializes the master instance.
* Initializes a standby master instance (if configured).
* Initializes the primary segment instances.
* Initializes the mirror segment instances (if mirroring is configured).
* Configures the Bizgres MPP system and checks for errors.
* Starts the Bizgres MPP system.


*****************************************************
OPTIONS
*****************************************************

-c <mpp_config_file>

Required. The full path and filename of the MPP configuration file, which 
contains all of the defined parameters to configure the array. See 
'mpp_config_example' for instructions on creating this file.

-h <host_file>

Optional. The full path and filename of a file that contains the host names 
of all the segment hosts in the array. If not specified on the command line, 
you can specify the host file using the MACHINE_LIST_FILE parameter in the 
mpp_config file.

-p <postgresql_conf_mpp_additions>

Optional. The name of a file that contains global postgresql.conf parameter 
settings that you want to set for Bizgres MPP. These settings will be used 
when the individual master and segment instances are initialized.

-s <standby_master_host>

Optional. If you wish to configure a backup master host, specify the host 
name using this option. If not specified on the command line, you can 
specify it using the STANDBY_HOSTNAME parameter in the mpp_config file.

-i

If a standby master host is configured, this will start the synchronization 
process between the primary and backup MPP master hosts. The default is to 
not start the synchronization process.

-o

Creates a master instance only. Does not configure any segment hosts.

-m <max_connections>

Sets the maximum number of client connections allowed to the MPP master. 
The default is 25.

-a

Do not prompt the user for confirmation.

-q

Run in quiet mode. Command output is not displayed on the screen, 
but is still written to the log file.

-l logfile_directory

The directory to write the log file. Defaults to ~/mppAdminLogs.

-?

Displays the online help.

-v

Displays the version, status, last updated date, and check sum of 
this script.

*****************************************************
EXAMPLES
*****************************************************

Initialize a Bizgres MPP array:

./mppcreatecluster.sh -c mpp_config


Initialize a Bizgres MPP array with a standby MPP master host:

./mppcreatecluster.sh -c mpp_config -s host09 -i



Display the online help for the mppcreatecluster.sh script:

./mppcreatecluster.sh -?

